      <activity id="2113291c-91f0-523c-8cf2-3341c56c0b5e" activityNameId="4e1c7b66-d337-56f4-976f-65d79fe0905c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Proteins, from grass, at fermentation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Proteins, from grass, at fermentation
The multioutput-process "grass, to fermentation" delivers the co-products Ethanol, 95% in H20, from grass",  "fibres from grass", and "proteins from grass". The allocation is based on economic criteria. The production of ethanol from grass is of no economical importance in the world.;
UUID: 414c1978-7b0c-3437-81ba-c9e384c8dd5f
Fermentation of grass including materials, energy uses, infrastructure, and emissions.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Production of ethanol from grass with the Saccharification and Simultanous Fermentation process.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: The production of ethanol from grass in Switzerland was 15000 hl in 2000.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_414c1978-7b0c-3437-81ba-c9e384c8dd5f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
